            <ArticleTitle>Successful surgical treatment of ventricular tachycardia that induced left ventricular aneurysm in 12-year-old boy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>53-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A surgical treatment of ventricular tachycardia (VT) that induced a congenital left ventricular aneurysm (LVA) in a 12-year-old boy was performed. The VT disappeared after epicardial cryoablation and a reinforcement of LVA with a composite patch. Epicardial cryoablation, based on an intraoperative electrophysiologic study (EPS), is effective in treating VT resistant to antiarrhythmia drugs.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
